Do you need to allow connection only from `testdb`, `test`, `db_111`, `db_110` and block any others?

In that case you need to set authentication to `block` for default:default user

```
database default {
	user default {
		authentication "block"
                ...
        }
}
```

@thedrow pgbouncer has been around for 11 years. No one has bothered to implement that feature either publicly or privately AFAIK.

Note that I'm talking about maintaining a prepared statement cache or whatever inside the daemon.

pgbouncer supports one shot prepared statements in transaction pooling mode. I'm assuming odyssey does too, but I don't think it did until this PR: https://github.com/yandex/odyssey/pull/20

